section('01  Project introduction')
add('inBox is a full-stack e-commerce application that brings shopping, order management, merchant operations and seller governance into one browser-based platform. Customers can browse a catalog, search and filter products, choose variants, save favorites, manage a cart and address book, obtain a server-calculated quote and place orders. Merchants receive a dedicated operations panel, while super administrators review seller applications and govern platform access.')
add('The project addresses a common commerce problem: product discovery, pricing, stock, customer accounts and fulfillment must remain consistent across multiple screens and user roles. Its architecture separates a React presentation layer from an Express API and PostgreSQL persistence. Prisma describes the relational model and supplies typed database access. The backend recalculates monetary values from stored product prices and reserves inventory through conditional updates inside transactions.')
h('Business purpose and intended users')
add('For shoppers, the platform provides a journey from product discovery to order tracking. For merchants, it centralizes inventory, imagery, fulfillment queues, customer information and revenue indicators. For platform operators, it provides seller application review, approval, rejection, suspension and administrator governance. Managers and judges can evaluate both the implemented workflows and the engineering evidence behind them.')
h('Implemented scope')
add('The interface includes a storefront, catalog, product details, cart, wishlist, checkout, order success and tracking, order history, profile, login, seller onboarding, merchant dashboard and super-admin dashboard. English, German and Dutch translation dictionaries are present. Stripe hosted checkout and Cash on Delivery use separate payment paths. Cloudinary supports product-image uploads when configured.')
h('Engineering approach')
add('The application uses browser-history navigation, React contexts for shared state, a fetch-based API client, cookie-backed sessions, role checks, REST-style modules, database constraints, and unit, mocked-service, component, browser and load-testing tools. The source includes Docker configurations, seed and backup utilities, and a GitHub Actions verification workflow.')
h('Evaluation position')
add('The implementation is suitable for a detailed project demonstration and engineering review. This report does not certify a production release: source inspection found payment-trust and seller-scope gaps, schema-to-migration drift and incomplete recovery evidence. Fresh test outcomes and older results are separated so reviewers can judge the actual state of the project.')
source('src/App.tsx; server/app.ts; prisma/schema.prisma; package.json; server/modules/*')
