section('07  Commerce workflows and rules')
h('Browse, quote and checkout')
add('Catalog search uses case-insensitive contains over product name, description and brand, with category equality filtering. Paging defaults to 50 and caps at 100. Sort values: featured, price_asc, price_desc, rating, newest. This is database filtering, not a dedicated full-text search engine.')
add('The quote service accepts up to 100 items with positive safe-integer quantities. It loads stored prices, excludes missing/archived/out-of-stock products, caps quantity to stock and returns warnings. Coupons support percentage discounts, minimum spend, optional caps, free shipping and usage limits. The schema has no coupon-expiry or fixed-amount-discount field.')
table(['RULE','IMPLEMENTATION'],[('Stored money','Integer minor units; serializers also expose major units.'),('Free/reduced shipping','Subtotal >=7500 minor units ($75), or free-shipping coupon.'),('Standard shipping','499 minor units below threshold; otherwise 0.'),('Express shipping','1299 minor units below threshold; otherwise 499.'),('Tax','Round 8% of max(0, subtotal - discount); application rule, not configurable tax engine.'),('Total','max(0, subtotal - discount) + delivery + tax; 0 for empty valid quote.'),('Currency','Order/Stripe creation uses USD. Display controls are not proof of multi-currency settlement.')],[125,374])
h('Inventory and order lifecycle')
add('POST /api/orders recomputes a quote, optionally compares expectedTotalMinor, and associates an idempotency key with a payload hash. A transaction conditionally decrements stock, records coupon use, writes order/item/address snapshots and status history, clears ordered cart products and saves the checkout record. Retry the same logical order with the same key; omitted keys generate new ones.')
add('Stages: Order Placed, Confirmed, Packed, Shipped, Out for Delivery, Delivered. Backward transitions are rejected; forward jumps are allowed. COD begins Pending, and an admin can collect payment. Stripe uses a separate pending-order/session flow and signed webhooks. Payment-integrity gaps are in section 21.')
source('server/modules/catalog; server/modules/checkout/pricingService.ts; server/modules/orders; server/modules/payments')
section('08  Database design and integrity')
add(f'The Prisma schema defines {len(models)} PostgreSQL models. IDs are text, generally uuid() defaults; Product.id is supplied by application/seed code. Media, variants and specifications use JSON. Monetary values use integer minor units. Role and SellerStatus are enums; payment and fulfillment states are strings enforced by application logic.')
table(['AREA','MODELS'],[('Identity and sellers','User, Session, Address, SellerApplication'),('Catalog and shopping','Product, CartItem, SavedItem, WishlistItem, Review'),('Checkout and orders','Order, OrderItem, OrderStatusHistory, CheckoutRequest'),('Marketing','Coupon, CouponRedemption, NewsletterSubscription'),('Infrastructure','HealthCheck')],[150,349])
h('Keys, ownership and deletion')
add('Unique keys protect user email, session token hash, coupon code, order number and checkout idempotency key. Cart/saved variants use userId + productId + selectedColor + selectedSize uniqueness. Wishlist is unique per user/product; Review per product/user. CheckoutRequest.orderId is optional and unique, giving an order at most one ledger record.')
add('User deletion cascades to sessions, addresses and shopping/review/checkout data, but orders use Restrict. Product deletion cascades to shopping/review rows and sets historical OrderItem.productId to null. SellerApplication.userId also uses SetNull. Order items/status history cascade with their order; coupon deletion is restricted by redemptions.')
h('Indexes and snapshots')
add('Indexes cover role, session expiry, owner IDs, category/archive flags, order user/date/status and review product/date. Shipping addresses and item names/prices are snapshots. CouponRedemption.orderId, SellerApplication.reviewedBy and OrderStatusHistory.actor are scalar fields, not declared foreign keys.')
note('<b>Migration gap:</b> The only checked-in migration defines Role with CUSTOMER and ADMIN and lacks newer seller application/status additions. The ER diagrams describe schema.prisma, not a verified live database. A clean installation using only prisma migrate deploy will not necessarily match the schema; a reviewed follow-up migration is required.')
source('prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations/20261019070107_init_commerce_schema/migration.sql')
