code('# Review/correct configuration before deploying.\ndocker compose -f compose.yaml config\ndocker compose -f compose.yaml up -d --build\ndocker compose -f compose.yaml logs --tail 100 app')
add('Both Compose files duplicate the stack. They declare postgres:18-alpine, a named volume, localhost database exposure, app port 4000 and health checks. Startup does not migrate/seed. The runner omits devDependencies but invokes npx prisma generate; validate CLI availability in a clean image. Verify the PostgreSQL 18 volume layout before relying on persistence. Docker was not run here.')
h('Monitoring')
add('Health/readiness routes and logs expose timestamp, requestId, method, URL, status and durationMs. Selected query secrets are redacted. Shutdown closes HTTP and disconnects Prisma. Central alerts/metrics storage were not verified.')
h('Backup and restore')
code('npm run db:backup\npg_dump -U postgres -d inbox_store -F c -f inbox_store.dump\n# Separate clean recovery database only:\npg_restore -U postgres -d inbox_store_recovery inbox_store.dump')
add('JSON backup exports nine model groups and checks structure/product counts; it does not restore data. It omits sessions, carts, saved/wishlist items, redemptions, checkout requests, seller applications and HealthCheck. Use full backups and a measured restore drill. Tracked backups may contain password hashes/personal data and were not reproduced.')
